{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RtXg9EegrLwrXLnRMjLWeT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Feature: Create hello.sh executable script\n\n## Description\nCreate a new executable Bash script `hello.sh` at the repository root that prints `Hello, World!` to stdout. This is the sole deliverable for the project — a greenfield addition with no modifications to existing files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `hello.sh` exists at the repository root\n- [ ] First line is exactly `#!/usr/bin/env bash`\n- [ ] Script body is `printf 'Hello, World!\\n'`\n- [ ] File uses LF line endings and plain ASCII text\n- [ ] Running `./hello.sh` outputs exactly `Hello, World!\\n` to stdout\n- [ ] Script exits with status `0`\n- [ ] Script writes nothing to stderr\n- [ ] File has the executable bit set on disk (`chmod +x`)\n- [ ] Git tracks the file with mode `100755`\n- [ ] No existing files are modified (README.md, .ralph/*, etc.)\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `hello.sh` - Create new file with shebang and printf command; set executable permission and stage with `git add --chmod=+x hello.sh`\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: none\n- Blocks: none (this is the only and final feature)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n1. Write the file with exactly two lines: the shebang and the printf statement.\n2. Ensure executable bit is recorded in Git via `git add --chmod=+x hello.sh`.\n3. Do **not** add tests, CI config, argument parsing, or any other files.\n\n## Verification\n```bash\ntest -x hello.sh\nhead -1 hello.sh | diff -u - <(printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n')\n./hello.sh | diff -u - <(printf 'Hello, World!\\n')\n./hello.sh >/dev/null; test \"$?\" -eq 0\nstderr=\"$(./hello.sh 2>&1 >/dev/null)\"; test -z \"$stderr\"\ngit ls-files -s hello.sh | grep -Eq '^100755 '\n```\n\n---"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":314,"cache_read_input_tokens":16572,"cache_creation":{"ephe